candidate_profile:
Position:
Automation QA Engineer

Moreinfo:
Junior Python Automation QA Engineer experienced in the testing of Embedded systems/devices. Currently, I'm working in one of the greatest outsourcing companies on the market.

In my current position I am responsible for:
- Analysis and review of functional and non-functional requirements;
- Functional and Performance, Ad-Hoc and Exploratory, Regression, Smoke, and Sanity testing;
- Creation of automated tests in Python in the confines of existing test framework means and tools;
- Creation and maintenance of automated scripts aiming for ease of project processes flow (automated e-mail reports, reports upload to Confluence, reports analysis, metrics collection from Jira, etc.);
- Extension of the existing test framework for new functionality testing or test environment parts support;
- Investigation, documenting, and detailed reporting of defects that occurred, confirmation testing upon the fix.

I'm familiar with working with tools and technologies:
- Python, Bash Shell, Git, Gerrit, and Jenkins for source code development, control, and continuous integration;
- Configuring Linux and Unix-like distributions (CentOS, Ubuntu), Yocto, OpenWrt, AndroidSDK as a part of the test environment for embedded systems testing;
- Jira, Mantis for defects reporting and tracking, Confluence for valuable knowledge sharing;
- Additionally, I was certified for a deeper knowledge of L2/L3 computer networking with HCNA and CCNA certificates, aware of 802.11 protocol details for L2 communication.

My other skills and qualifications include:
- Confident communication in both written and spoken English;
- Strong commitment towards work, thoughtfulness in everything I do, which drives my constant self-improvement, proneness for experimenting while looking for the best resolution of a problem;
- I'm greatly attentive to details, know prioritizing my tasks in the most beneficial for the order of the current goals and quickly adapt myself to changes in workload, responsibilities, or tools to work with.

In general, I'm an open-minded and easy-going team member; communication and collaboration are great with me, because I'm an active listener, empath, and optimist, who often tends to mediation, either when collaborating or resolving any arising issues inside the team.

English Level:
upper

Experience Years:
1.5

